      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this change is dangerous, because it will recompute the diff much more often than the user would like and thus resetting the entire diff.\n\nThis is how `keyLocations$` is computed:\n```\n  readonly keyLocations$: Observable\u003cKeyLocations\u003e \u003d select(\n    this.state$,\n    diffState \u003d\u003e\n      computeKeyLocations(diffState.lineOfInterest, diffState.comments ?? [])\n  );\n```\n\nThis means that any diffState change will trigger the observable to fire.\n\nAlso `diffState.comments` may change all the time (new comment, changed comments, ...).\n\nSo I think this change needs very careful and thorough testing.",
